  "student_passage": "### A\n\nMy aunt runs a bakery (1) ____ opens at seven every morning. Yesterday she put three small (2) ____ (cake) in the window. They were (3) ____ (cheap) than the large cakes on the shelf. I wrote their prices as (4) ____ (clear) as I could. Before leaving, I checked that each price was beside the correct cake.\n\n### B\n\nOur art teacher brought an old painting to class. The colours were (5) ____ (bright) than I had expected. She told us (6) ____ look at the shadows before mixing our paints. I had always been afraid (7) ____ making mistakes, but she explained that we could let the paper dry and try again on another sheet.\n\n### C\n\nAt the station we saw a passenger (8) ____ (push) a red bicycle towards the lift. He was the man (9) ____ ticket my brother had found on a bench. We returned it to him before the train arrived. He thanked us for (10) ____ (return) it. We were glad that a small discovery had solved his problem.",
